Band Description: A four-piece ensemble that performs exclusively on "reclaimed" stages, often consisting of stacks of rusted shipping containers. The lead singer, a former radio technician named Elara, uses a vintage vocoder to weave the desert wind into her lyrics, while the guitarist, Kael, plays with a slide made from a hollowed-out cactus spine. Their aesthetic is "industrial-ascetic"—utilizing goggles and torn, sand-colored techwear, creating a stage presence that feels both like a technical repair session and a religious trance.

